/-!
# A conormal sheaf of rank `c` cuts the subscheme out by `c` equations

Let `i : Z ⟶ X` be a closed immersion of finite presentation whose conormal sheaf
`𝒞_{Z/X} = ℐ/ℐ²` is finite locally free of rank `c`.  This file proves that every point of the
image has an affine open neighbourhood `W` on which the ideal sheaf of `Z` is generated by
*exactly* `c` sections `f₁, …, f_c ∈ Γ(X, W)`, and — when `c ≠ 0` — that such charts cover all
of `X`.

The count is tied to the rank throughout: no statement below produces "some number" of
equations.

## Main results

* `Ideal.eq_span_of_span_range_toCotangent_eq_top`: **Nakayama read on `I/I²`.**  Elements of a
  finitely generated ideal `I` of a local ring, contained in the maximal ideal, whose classes
  span `I/I²` generate `I`.  This is the form the conormal sheaf delivers its rank in, the
  stalk of the conormal sheaf being `I/I²` and not `I/𝔪I`.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ConormalEquations.exists_stalkIdeal_eq_span_of_conormalRank`: the
  stalk of the ideal sheaf at a point of the image is generated by `c` elements.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ConormalEquations.exists_affineOpen_equations_of_conormalRank`:
  **the local `c` equations.**  An affine open `W` around a point of the image and
  `f : Fin c → Γ(X, W)` generating the ideal sheaf of `Z` on `W`, stated both as
  `IsGeneratedByOn` and, read on sections, as `RingHom.ker (i.app W).hom = Ideal.span (range f)`.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ConormalEquations.exists_basis_idealCotangentFiber_of_conormalRank`:
  **the count is exactly `c`.**  The cotangent fibre `ℐ_x / 𝔪_x ℐ_x` at a point of the image has
  a basis indexed by `Fin c`, the classes of `c` generators of `ℐ_x`; equivalently, `ℐ_x` cannot
  be generated by fewer than `c` elements.  This is the shape [Stacks, Tag 067N] consumes.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ConormalEquations.exists_equationCharts_of_conormalRank`: the same
  data as a family of charts covering `X`, in the shape
  `AlgebraicGeometry.GysinChartData` consumes it — `ambient`, `equations`, `equations_vanish`,
  and `ambient_cover`, the last in the stronger form "the chart of `p` contains `p`".  Here
  `c ≠ 0` is needed and is not a defect of the proof: for `c = 0` a point outside `Z` has no
  neighbourhood on which the unit ideal is generated by the empty family.

## Implementation notes

The chain is: local freeness of rank `c` gives a basis of the stalk of the conormal sheaf
indexed by `Fin c` (`AlgebraicGeometry.nonempty_stalkBasis_of_isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank`); the
stalk of the conormal sheaf is the cotangent module `I/I²` of the kernel `I` of the map of local
rings of the canonical closed factor (`Stacks.Conormal.conormalSheafStalkEquivCotangent`), so
`I/I²` is spanned by `c` elements; Nakayama in the `I/I²` form above turns that into `c`
generators of `I`; the identification of local rings with those of the coborder
neighbourhood transports the generators to the stalk of the defining ideal sheaf on `X`; and
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.exists_isGeneratedByOn_definingIdealOfHom` spreads
them out to a neighbourhood, which is then shrunk to an affine one.  On an affine open
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ker_app_eq_span_range` reads the resulting generation off sections.

The scalars on the stalk of the conormal sheaf are the local ring of `Z`, while Nakayama runs
over the local ring of the coborder neighbourhood; `span_eq_top_of_span_eq_top_of_surjective`
is the passage between the two, through the surjection of the one onto the other.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0G86](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0G86)
* [Stacks Project, Lemma 10.20.1 (Tag 00DV)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00DV)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01C6](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01C6)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory Opposite TopologicalSpace
open Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorStalkRingedSpace

universe u

/-! ### Nakayama in the cotangent form -/

/-- **Nakayama's lemma read on `I/I²`.**  Let `I` be a finitely generated ideal of a local ring
`R`, contained in the maximal ideal.  Finitely many elements of `I` whose classes span the
cotangent module `I/I²` generate `I`.

This is the shape in which a conormal sheaf delivers a generator count: its stalk is `I/I²`,
whereas `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.stalkIdeal_eq_span_of_span_idealCotangentFiber`
asks for a spanning family of `I/𝔪I`. -/
theorem Ideal.eq_span_of_span_range_toCotangent_eq_top {R : Type u} [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R]
    {I : Ideal R} (hIm : I ≤ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R) (hfg : I.FG) {n : ℕ} (f : Fin n → I)
    (hspan : Submodule.span R (Set.range fun a => I.toCotangent (f a)) = ⊤) :
    I = Ideal.span (Set.range fun a => (f a : R)) := by
  classical
  have hsq : I ^ 2 ≤ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R • I := by
    rw [pow_two, Ideal.smul_eq_mul]
    exact Ideal.mul_mono hIm le_rfl
  refine le_antisymm ?_ (Ideal.span_le.mpr ?_)
  · refine Submodule.le_of_le_smul_of_le_jacobson_bot
      (I := IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R) hfg
      (le_of_eq (IsLocalRing.jacobson_eq_maximalIdeal (⊥ : Ideal R) bot_ne_top).symm)
      fun a ha => ?_
    have hmem : I.toCotangent ⟨a, ha⟩ ∈ Submodule.span R
        (Set.range fun b => I.toCotangent (f b)) := by
      simp [hspan]
    obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := (Submodule.mem_span_range_iff_exists_fun _).mp hmem
    have h0 : I.toCotangent ((⟨a, ha⟩ : I) - ∑ b, c b • f b) = 0 := by
      rw [map_sub, map_sum, sub_eq_zero, ← hc]
      exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun b _ => map_smul I.toCotangent (c b) (f b)
    have hcoe : (((⟨a, ha⟩ : I) - ∑ b, c b • f b : I) : R)
        = a - ∑ b, c b * (f b : R) := by
      rw [Submodule.coe_sub, AddSubmonoidClass.coe_finsetSum]
      rfl
    have hmem2 : a - ∑ b, c b * (f b : R) ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R • I := by
      refine hsq ?_
      rw [← hcoe]
      exact (I.toCotangent_eq_zero _).mp h0
    refine Submodule.mem_sup.mpr ⟨∑ b, c b * (f b : R), ?_, a - ∑ b, c b * (f b : R),
      hmem2, by ring⟩
    exact Submodule.sum_mem _ fun b _ =>
      Ideal.mul_mem_left _ _ (Ideal.subset_span ⟨b, rfl⟩)
  · rintro _ ⟨b, rfl⟩
    exact (f b).2

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ConormalEquations

/-! ### Changing the scalars of a spanning family -/

/-- **A spanning family stays spanning when the scalars are replaced by a ring surjecting onto
them.**  Let `M` carry module structures over `R` and over `S` and let `σ : R → S` be a
surjective ring map with `σ r • m = r • m`.  A set spanning `M` over `S` spans it over `R`. -/
theorem span_eq_top_of_span_eq_top_of_surjective {R S M : Type u} [CommRing R] [CommRing S]
    [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M] [Module S M] (σ : R →+* S) (hσ : Function.Surjective σ)
    (hcompat : ∀ (r : R) (m : M), σ r • m = r • m) {T : Set M}
    (hT : Submodule.span S T = ⊤) : Submodule.span R T = ⊤ := by
  have key : ∀ m : M, m ∈ Submodule.span S T → m ∈ Submodule.span R T := by
    intro m hmem
    induction hmem using Submodule.span_induction with
    | mem x hx => exact Submodule.subset_span hx
    | zero => exact zero_mem _
    | add x y _ _ hx hy => exact add_mem hx hy
    | smul s x _ hx =>
      obtain ⟨r, rfl⟩ := hσ s
      rw [hcompat]
      exact Submodule.smul_mem _ r hx
  exact top_le_iff.mp fun m _ => key m (by simp [hT])

/-! ### A free cotangent module bounds the number of generators from below -/

/-- **An ideal whose cotangent module is free of rank `c` needs at least `c` generators.**  Let
`E : R ≃+* A` be an isomorphism of rings carrying an ideal `J` of `R` to an ideal `I` of `A`, let
`S` be a ring onto which `A` surjects, and suppose `I/I²` is free of rank `c` over `S` — the
situation of a conormal sheaf of rank `c`, where `A` is the local ring of the coborder
neighbourhood, `S` the local ring of the closed subscheme and `I/I²` the stalk of the conormal
sheaf.  Then `J` cannot be generated by fewer than `c` elements.

Each step is a comparison of minimal numbers of generators, `Submodule.spanFinrank`: a free
module of rank `c` needs `c` generators; replacing the scalars `S` by the ring `A` surjecting
onto them changes nothing; the quotient `I ⟶ I/I²` needs no more than its source; and the
isomorphism `E` carries generators of `J` to generators of `I`. -/
theorem le_spanFinrank_of_basis_cotangent {R A S : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing A] [CommRing S]
    [Nontrivial S] [Algebra A S] (hσ : Function.Surjective (algebraMap A S)) (E : R ≃+* A)
    {J : Ideal R}
    {I : Ideal A} (hI : Ideal.map E J = I) (hJ : J.FG) {c : ℕ} [Module S I.Cotangent]
    [IsScalarTower A S I.Cotangent] (b : Module.Basis (Fin c) S I.Cotangent) :
    c ≤ J.spanFinrank := by
  classical
  have hIfg : I.FG := by
    obtain ⟨T, hTfin, hT⟩ := Submodule.fg_def.mp hJ
    rw [← hI, ← hT, Ideal.map_span]
    exact Submodule.fg_def.mpr ⟨E '' T, hTfin.image _, rfl⟩
  have : Module.Free S I.Cotangent := Module.Free.of_basis b
  -- The minimal number of generators does not change when the scalars `S` are replaced by `A`.
  have hres : (⊤ : Submodule A I.Cotangent).spanRank
      = (⊤ : Submodule S I.Cotangent).spanRank := by
    rw [← Submodule.restrictScalars_top (S := A) (R := S) (M := I.Cotangent)]
    exact Submodule.spanRank_restrictScalars_eq hσ ⊤
  -- The quotient `I ⟶ I/I²` needs no more generators than `I` does.
  have hquot : (Submodule.map I.toCotangent (⊤ : Submodule A I)).spanFinrank
      ≤ (⊤ : Submodule A I).spanFinrank :=
    Submodule.spanFinrank_map_le_of_fg I.toCotangent ((Submodule.fg_top I).mpr hIfg)
  rw [Submodule.map_top, I.toCotangent_range] at hquot
  calc c = (⊤ : Submodule S I.Cotangent).spanFinrank := by
        rw [← Module.finrank_eq_spanFinrank_of_free, Module.finrank_eq_card_basis b,
          Fintype.card_fin]
    _ = (⊤ : Submodule A I.Cotangent).spanFinrank := congrArg Cardinal.toNat hres.symm
    _ ≤ (⊤ : Submodule A I).spanFinrank := hquot
    _ = I.spanFinrank := Submodule.spanFinrank_top I
    _ = J.spanFinrank := by rw [← hI, Ideal.spanFinrank_map_eq_of_ringEquiv]

/-! ### `c` generators of the stalk of the ideal sheaf -/

section Stalk

open Stacks.Conormal Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf Stacks.RingedSpace

attribute [local instance] Stacks.Conormal.idealSheafStalkModule
  Stacks.Conormal.conormalSheafStalkModule Stacks.Conormal.stalkMapAlgebra
  Stacks.Conormal.cotangentStalkModule

variable {Z X : Scheme.{u}} (i : Z ⟶ X) [IsImmersion i] (c : ℕ) (z : Z)

/-- Finite local freeness of rank `c` of the conormal sheaf of `i`, at the spelling of the base
sheaf of rings that `Stacks.Conormal.conormalSheaf` is declared over. -/
abbrev ConormalRank : Prop :=
  SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u}
    (R := structureSheafRing Z.toRingedSpace) (Stacks.Conormal.conormalSheaf i) c

/-- **The stalk of a rank-`c` conormal sheaf has a basis indexed by `Fin c`, at the spelling of
the module structure the cotangent identification is stated over.**
`AlgebraicGeometry.nonempty_stalkBasis_of_isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank` delivers the basis over
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorStalkRingedSpace.stalkModule`, while
`Stacks.Conormal.conormalSheafStalkEquivCotangent` is linear over
`Stacks.Conormal.conormalSheafStalkModule`.  The two are equal as instances — that is
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.stalkModule_eq` — but instance search does not cross the gap, so the
equality is applied here once and for all. -/
theorem nonempty_conormalStalkBasis (hE : ConormalRank i c) :
    Nonempty (@Module.Basis (Fin c) (ToType (Z.presheaf.stalk z))
      (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := Ab.{u})
        (Stacks.Conormal.conormalSheaf i).val.presheaf z)) _ _
      (conormalSheafStalkModule i z)) := by
  rw [show conormalSheafStalkModule i z
      = Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorStalkRingedSpace.stalkModule Z.toRingedSpace
        (Stacks.Conormal.conormalSheaf i).val z from
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.stalkModule_eq Z.toRingedSpace
      (Stacks.Conormal.conormalSheaf i).val z).symm]
  exact AlgebraicGeometry.nonempty_stalkBasis_of_isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank
    (X := Z) (Stacks.Conormal.conormalSheaf i) c hE z

/-- **The two module structures on the local cotangent module agree.**  The local ring of `Z` at
`z` acts on `I/I²`, for `I` the kernel of the map of local rings of the canonical closed factor,
through the identification of that local ring with the quotient by `I`; so a scalar coming from
the local ring of the coborder neighbourhood acts in the same way whether it is first mapped
down or not. -/
theorem cotangentStalk_smul_eq
    (r : ToType (i.coborderRange.toScheme.presheaf.stalk (i.liftCoborder.base z)))
    (m : (RingHom.ker (i.liftCoborder.stalkMap z).hom).Cotangent) :
    (i.liftCoborder.stalkMap z).hom r • m = r • m := by
  show (RingHom.quotientKerEquivOfSurjective
    (i.liftCoborder.stalkMap_surjective z)).symm
      ((i.liftCoborder.stalkMap z).hom r) • m = r • m
  rw [RingHom.quotientKerEquivOfSurjective_symm_apply, ← Ideal.Quotient.algebraMap_eq,
    algebraMap_smul]

/-- **A conormal sheaf of rank `c` spans the local cotangent module by `c` elements.**  Write
`I` for the kernel of the map of local rings of the canonical closed factor `i.liftCoborder` at
`z`.  Then `I/I²` is spanned by the classes of `c` elements of `I`.

The stalk of the conormal sheaf is `I/I²`, and a sheaf finite locally free of rank `c` has a
stalk with a basis indexed by `Fin c`; the scalars of that basis are the local ring of `Z`,
which the local ring of the coborder neighbourhood surjects onto. -/
theorem exists_span_range_toCotangent_eq_top_of_conormalRank (hE : ConormalRank i c) :
    ∃ f : Fin c → RingHom.ker (i.liftCoborder.stalkMap z).hom,
      Submodule.span (ToType (i.coborderRange.toScheme.presheaf.stalk (i.liftCoborder.base z)))
          (Set.range fun a =>
            (RingHom.ker (i.liftCoborder.stalkMap z).hom).toCotangent (f a)) = ⊤ := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨b₀⟩ := nonempty_conormalStalkBasis i c z hE
  -- Transport the basis along the identification of the stalk with `I/I²`.
  set b := b₀.map (conormalSheafStalkEquivCotangent i z)
  -- Lift the spanning family through the quotient map `I ⟶ I/I²`.
  choose f hf using fun a =>
    (RingHom.ker (i.liftCoborder.stalkMap z).hom).toCotangent_surjective (b a)
  refine ⟨f, span_eq_top_of_span_eq_top_of_surjective (i.liftCoborder.stalkMap z).hom
    (i.liftCoborder.stalkMap_surjective z) (cotangentStalk_smul_eq i z) ?_⟩
  rw [show (Set.range fun a =>
      (RingHom.ker (i.liftCoborder.stalkMap z).hom).toCotangent (f a))
    = Set.range b from congrArg Set.range (funext hf)]
  exact b.span_eq

/-- The kernel of the map of local rings of the canonical closed factor is a proper ideal. -/
theorem ker_stalkMap_liftCoborder_le_maximalIdeal :
    RingHom.ker (i.liftCoborder.stalkMap z).hom ≤
      IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal
        (ToType (i.coborderRange.toScheme.presheaf.stalk (i.liftCoborder.base z))) :=
  IsLocalRing.le_maximalIdeal (RingHom.ker_ne_top _)

/-- The identification of the local ring of `X` at `i z` with that of the coborder
neighbourhood, as a ring isomorphism. -/
abbrev coborderStalkRingEquiv : ToType (X.presheaf.stalk (i.base z)) ≃+*
    ToType (i.coborderRange.toScheme.presheaf.stalk (i.liftCoborder.base z)) :=
  (coborderStalkEquiv i z).commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv

/-- The identification of local rings carries the stalk of the defining ideal sheaf to the
kernel of the map of local rings of the canonical closed factor. -/
theorem comap_ker_stalkMap_liftCoborder :
    Ideal.comap (coborderStalkRingEquiv i z) (RingHom.ker (i.liftCoborder.stalkMap z).hom) =
      stalkIdeal (X := X.toLocallyRingedSpace) (definingIdealOfHom i) (i.base z) := by
  rw [stalkIdeal_definingIdealOfHom_eq_ker i z]
  refine Submodule.ext fun a => ?_
  rw [Ideal.mem_comap, RingHom.mem_ker, RingHom.mem_ker]
  exact Iff.of_eq (congrArg (fun t => t = 0) (stalkMap_coborderStalkEquiv i z a))

/-- The same identification read forwards: the stalk of the defining ideal sheaf is carried onto
the kernel of the map of local rings of the canonical closed factor. -/
theorem map_coborderStalkRingEquiv_stalkIdeal :
    Ideal.map (coborderStalkRingEquiv i z)
        (stalkIdeal (X := X.toLocallyRingedSpace) (definingIdealOfHom i) (i.base z)) =
      RingHom.ker (i.liftCoborder.stalkMap z).hom := by
  rw [← comap_ker_stalkMap_liftCoborder i z,
    Ideal.map_comap_of_surjective _ (coborderStalkRingEquiv i z).surjective]

/-- **Stalkwise `c` equations.**  For an immersion whose conormal sheaf is finite locally free
of rank `c`, the stalk of the defining ideal sheaf at a point of the image is generated by `c`
elements, provided that stalk is finitely generated.

Nakayama in the form `Ideal.eq_span_of_span_range_toCotangent_eq_top` turns the `c` elements
spanning the local cotangent module into `c` generators of the kernel on the coborder
neighbourhood, and the identification of local rings transports them to `X`. -/
theorem exists_stalkIdeal_eq_span_of_conormalRank (hE : ConormalRank i c)
    (hfg : (stalkIdeal (X := X.toLocallyRingedSpace) (definingIdealOfHom i) (i.base z)).FG) :
    ∃ g : Fin c → ToType (X.presheaf.stalk (i.base z)),
      stalkIdeal (X := X.toLocallyRingedSpace) (definingIdealOfHom i) (i.base z)
        = Ideal.span (Set.range g) := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨f, hf⟩ := exists_span_range_toCotangent_eq_top_of_conormalRank i c z hE
  set E := coborderStalkRingEquiv i z with hEdef
  -- The kernel on the coborder is finitely generated, being the image of a finitely generated
  -- ideal under the identification of local rings.
  have hkerfg : (RingHom.ker (i.liftCoborder.stalkMap z).hom).FG := by
    obtain ⟨S, hSfin, hS⟩ := Submodule.fg_def.mp hfg
    rw [← map_coborderStalkRingEquiv_stalkIdeal i z, ← hS, Ideal.map_span]
    exact Submodule.fg_def.mpr ⟨E '' S, hSfin.image _, rfl⟩
  -- Nakayama on the coborder.
  have hgen := Ideal.eq_span_of_span_range_toCotangent_eq_top
    (ker_stalkMap_liftCoborder_le_maximalIdeal i z) hkerfg f hf
  have h1 : Ideal.map E.symm (RingHom.ker (i.liftCoborder.stalkMap z).hom)
      = Ideal.map E.symm (Ideal.span (Set.range fun a =>
        ((f a : ToType (i.coborderRange.toScheme.presheaf.stalk (i.liftCoborder.base z)))))) :=
    congrArg (Ideal.map E.symm) hgen
  refine ⟨fun a => E.symm (f a : _), ?_⟩
  rw [← comap_ker_stalkMap_liftCoborder i z, ← hEdef, ← Ideal.map_symm, h1, Ideal.map_span,
    ← Set.range_comp]
  rfl

end Stalk

/-! ### `c` equations on an affine open -/

section Sections

open Stacks.Conormal Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf Stacks.RingedSpace

/-- **Finitely many elements of the stalk of an ideal subsheaf are germs of sections of that
subsheaf over one neighbourhood.** -/
theorem exists_sections_germ_eq {W : LocallyRingedSpace.{u}}
    (J : (structureSheafModule W.toRingedSpace).Submodule) {w : W} {n : ℕ}
    (a : Fin n → W.presheaf.stalk w) (ha : ∀ b, a b ∈ stalkIdeal J w) :
    ∃ (U : Opens W) (hw : w ∈ U) (s : Fin n → W.presheaf.obj (op U)),
      (∀ b, s b ∈ J.obj (op U)) ∧ ∀ b, W.presheaf.germ U w hw (s b) = a b := by
  classical
  choose U hU s hsg using fun b => (mem_stalkIdeal_iff J).mp (ha b)
  obtain ⟨V, hwV, hle⟩ := Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_nbhd_le (x := w) U hU
  exact ⟨V, hwV, fun b => W.presheaf.map (homOfLE (hle b)).op (s b),
    fun b => restrict_mem J _ (hsg b).1,
    fun b => (TopCat.Presheaf.germ_res_apply W.presheaf (homOfLE (hle b)) w hwV (s b)).trans
      (hsg b).2⟩

variable {Z X : Scheme.{u}} (i : Z ⟶ X)

/-- **The stalk of the defining ideal sheaf of a closed immersion of finite presentation is
finitely generated.**  Over an affine open the ideal is the kernel of the map on sections,
finitely generated by [Stacks, Tag 01TV]; its generators generate the ideal sheaf there, hence
each of its stalks. -/
theorem fg_stalkIdeal_definingIdealOfHom [IsClosedImmersion i]
    [LocallyOfFinitePresentation i] (x : X) :
    (stalkIdeal (X := X.toLocallyRingedSpace) (definingIdealOfHom i) x).FG := by
  obtain ⟨V, hV, hxV, -⟩ :=
    exists_isAffineOpen_mem_and_subset (X := X) (x := x) (U := ⊤) trivial
  have hfg : (i.ker.ideal ⟨V, hV⟩).FG :=
    (locallyOfFinitePresentation_iff_fg_ker i).mp inferInstance ⟨V, hV⟩
  obtain ⟨r, g, hg⟩ := Submodule.fg_iff_exists_fin_generating_family.mp hfg
  have hker : RingHom.ker (i.app V).hom = Ideal.span (Set.range g) :=
    (Scheme.Hom.ker_apply i ⟨V, hV⟩).symm.trans hg.symm
  exact stalkIdeal_fg_of_isGeneratedByOn (definingIdealOfHom i) V g
    (Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.isGeneratedByOn_definingIdealOfHom_of_ker_app_eq_span i hV g hker)
    x hxV

/-- **Away from the image of a closed immersion the subscheme is cut out by `c` units.**  Around
a point outside the image the defining ideal sheaf is the unit ideal, and for any `c ≠ 0` the
constant family `1, …, 1` of length `c` generates it on an affine open neighbourhood.

The hypothesis `c ≠ 0` cannot be dropped: the empty family generates the zero ideal, not the
unit ideal, on every nonempty open. -/
theorem exists_affineOpen_unit_equations [IsClosedImmersion i] (c : ℕ) (hc : c ≠ 0) {p : X}
    (hp : p ∉ Set.range i.base) :
    ∃ (W : X.Opens) (_ : IsAffineOpen W) (_ : p ∈ W),
      (∀ _ : Fin c, (1 : Γ(X, W)) ∈ (definingIdealOfHom i).obj (op W)) ∧
        IsGeneratedByOn X.toRingedSpace (definingIdealOfHom i) W (fun _ : Fin c => 1) ∧
        RingHom.ker (i.app W).hom
          = Ideal.span (Set.range (fun _ : Fin c => (1 : Γ(X, W)))) := by
  obtain ⟨W, hW, hpW, hWc⟩ := exists_isAffineOpen_mem_and_subset (X := X) (x := p)
    (U := ⟨(Set.range i.base)ᶜ, i.isClosedEmbedding.isClosed_range.isOpen_compl⟩) hp
  have hzero : ∀ (V : X.Opens), V ≤ W → ∀ t : Γ(X, V), (i.app V).hom t = 0 := by
    intro V hVW t
    have hpre : i ⁻¹ᵁ V = ⊥ := by
      refine le_bot_iff.mp fun w hw => ?_
      have hw' : i.base w ∈ V := hw
      exact absurd (Set.mem_range_self w) (hWc (hVW hw'))
    have : Subsingleton Γ(Z, i ⁻¹ᵁ V) := by
      rw [hpre]
      infer_instance
    exact Subsingleton.elim _ _
  have hWgen : IsGeneratedByOn X.toRingedSpace (definingIdealOfHom i) W
      (fun _ : Fin c => (1 : Γ(X, W))) := by
    intro V hVW
    have hJ : (definingIdealOfHom i).obj (op V) = ⊤ :=
      Submodule.eq_top_iff'.mpr fun t =>
        (mem_definingIdealOfHom_iff_app i V t).mpr (hzero V hVW t)
    have hG : (generatedIdealOn X.toRingedSpace W
        (fun _ : Fin c => (1 : Γ(X, W)))).obj (op V) = ⊤ := by
      refine Submodule.eq_top_iff'.mpr fun t => ?_
      refine (mem_generatedIdealOn_iff W _ V hVW t).mpr fun y hy => ?_
      have h1 : (1 : X.presheaf.stalk y) ∈ Jid (germFamily X.toRingedSpace W
          (fun _ : Fin c => (1 : Γ(X, W))) y (hVW hy)) :=
        Ideal.subset_span ⟨⟨0, Nat.pos_of_ne_zero hc⟩, map_one _⟩
      rw [(Ideal.eq_top_iff_one _).mpr h1]
      exact Submodule.mem_top
    rw [hJ, hG]
  exact ⟨W, hW, hpW,
    fun _ => (mem_definingIdealOfHom_iff_app i W (1 : Γ(X, W))).mpr (hzero W le_rfl 1), hWgen,
    Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ker_app_eq_span_range i hW _ hWgen⟩

/-- **Rank-`c` conormal sheaf implies `c` local equations.**  Let `i : Z ⟶ X` be a closed
immersion of finite presentation whose conormal sheaf is finite locally free of rank `c`.  Then
every point of `Z` has an affine open neighbourhood `W` in `X` carrying `c` sections
`f₁, …, f_c ∈ Γ(X, W)` of the ideal sheaf of `Z` which generate it on `W`: on `W` the closed
subscheme `Z` is cut out by exactly `c` equations.  The last clause is the same statement read on
sections, `Z ∩ W = V(f₁, …, f_c)` as an equality of ideals of `Γ(X, W)`.

This is the step that produces the equation charts assumed by [Stacks, Tag 0G86]. -/
theorem exists_affineOpen_equations_of_conormalRank [IsClosedImmersion i]
    [LocallyOfFinitePresentation i] (c : ℕ) (hE : ConormalRank i c) (z : Z) :
    ∃ (W : X.Opens) (_ : IsAffineOpen W) (_ : i.base z ∈ W) (f : Fin c → Γ(X, W)),
      (∀ a, f a ∈ (definingIdealOfHom i).obj (op W)) ∧
        IsGeneratedByOn X.toRingedSpace (definingIdealOfHom i) W f ∧
        RingHom.ker (i.app W).hom = Ideal.span (Set.range f) := by
  obtain ⟨g, hg⟩ := exists_stalkIdeal_eq_span_of_conormalRank i c z hE
    (fg_stalkIdeal_definingIdealOfHom i (i.base z))
  have hgmem : ∀ a, g a ∈ stalkIdeal (X := X.toLocallyRingedSpace) (definingIdealOfHom i)
      (i.base z) := fun a => hg ▸ Ideal.subset_span ⟨a, rfl⟩
  obtain ⟨U, hxU, s, hsJ, hsg⟩ :=
    exists_sections_germ_eq (W := X.toLocallyRingedSpace) (definingIdealOfHom i) g hgmem
  have hgen : stalkIdeal (X := X.toLocallyRingedSpace) (definingIdealOfHom i) (i.base z)
      = Jid (germFamily X.toRingedSpace U s (i.base z) hxU) := by
    rw [hg]
    exact congrArg Ideal.span (congrArg Set.range (funext fun a => (hsg a).symm))
  obtain ⟨U', hxU', hU'U, hgen'⟩ := exists_isGeneratedByOn_definingIdealOfHom i
    (subset_coborder ⟨z, rfl⟩) hxU s hsJ hgen
  obtain ⟨W, hW, hxW, hWU'0⟩ :=
    exists_isAffineOpen_mem_and_subset (X := X) (x := i.base z) (U := U') hxU'
  have hWU' : W ≤ U' := hWU'0
  have hcomp : (fun a => X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hWU').op
        (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hU'U).op (s a)))
      = fun a => X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (hWU'.trans hU'U)).op (s a) := by
    funext a
    rw [← CommRingCat.comp_apply, ← Functor.map_comp]
    rfl
  have hWgen : IsGeneratedByOn X.toRingedSpace (definingIdealOfHom i) W
      (fun a => X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (hWU'.trans hU'U)).op (s a)) :=
    hcomp ▸ isGeneratedByOn_of_le U' (fun a => X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hU'U).op (s a))
      hgen' W hWU'
  exact ⟨W, hW, hxW, fun a => X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (hWU'.trans hU'U)).op (s a),
    fun a => restrict_mem _ _ (hsJ a), hWgen,
    Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ker_app_eq_span_range i hW _ hWgen⟩

/-- **The equation charts of [Stacks, Tag 0G86].**  For a closed immersion `i : Z ⟶ X` of finite
presentation with conormal sheaf finite locally free of rank `c ≠ 0`, the whole of `X` is covered
by affine opens on each of which `Z` is cut out by exactly `c` equations.  The data is returned
in the shape `AlgebraicGeometry.GysinChartData` consumes: `ambient`, `equations`,
`equations_vanish` (the third clause) and `ambient_cover` (the second clause, with the chart of
`p` containing `p`).

The hypothesis `c ≠ 0` is used only for the charts away from `Z`, where the ideal sheaf is the
unit ideal and the `c` equations are taken to be `1`; it cannot be dropped, since for `c = 0` the
empty family generates the zero ideal, not the unit ideal, on every nonempty open. -/
theorem exists_equationCharts_of_conormalRank [IsClosedImmersion i]
    [LocallyOfFinitePresentation i] (c : ℕ) (hE : ConormalRank i c) (hc : c ≠ 0) :
    ∃ (ambient : X → X.Opens) (equations : (p : X) → Fin c → Γ(X, ambient p)),
      (∀ p, IsAffineOpen (ambient p)) ∧ (∀ p, p ∈ ambient p) ∧
        (∀ (p : X) (V : X.Opens) (hV : V ≤ ambient p) (j : Fin c),
          (i.app V).hom (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hV).op (equations p j)) = 0) ∧
        (∀ p, IsGeneratedByOn X.toRingedSpace (definingIdealOfHom i)
          (ambient p) (equations p)) ∧
        ∀ p, RingHom.ker (i.app (ambient p)).hom = Ideal.span (Set.range (equations p)) := by
  classical
  have key : ∀ p : X, ∃ (W : X.Opens) (_ : IsAffineOpen W) (_ : p ∈ W) (f : Fin c → Γ(X, W)),
      (∀ a, f a ∈ (definingIdealOfHom i).obj (op W)) ∧
        IsGeneratedByOn X.toRingedSpace (definingIdealOfHom i) W f ∧
        RingHom.ker (i.app W).hom = Ideal.span (Set.range f) := by
    -- At a point of `Z` this is the local statement; away from `Z` the ideal sheaf is the unit
    -- ideal, generated by the constant family `1`.
    intro p
    by_cases hp : p ∈ Set.range i.base
    · obtain ⟨z, rfl⟩ := hp
      exact exists_affineOpen_equations_of_conormalRank i c hE z
    · obtain ⟨W, hW, hpW, hmem, hWgen, hWker⟩ :=
        exists_affineOpen_unit_equations i c hc hp
      exact ⟨W, hW, hpW, fun _ => 1, hmem, hWgen, hWker⟩
  choose ambient hamb hmem equations hvanish hgen hspan using key
  exact ⟨ambient, equations, hamb, hmem, fun p V hV j =>
    (mem_definingIdealOfHom_iff_app i V _).mp
      (restrict_mem (definingIdealOfHom i) (homOfLE hV) (hvanish p j)), hgen, hspan⟩

end Sections

/-! ### A basis of the cotangent fibre -/

section CotangentFibreBasis

open Stacks.Conormal Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf Stacks.RingedSpace

attribute [local instance] Stacks.Conormal.idealSheafStalkModule
  Stacks.Conormal.conormalSheafStalkModule Stacks.Conormal.stalkMapAlgebra
  Stacks.Conormal.cotangentStalkModule

variable {Z X : Scheme.{u}} (i : Z ⟶ X) [IsClosedImmersion i] [LocallyOfFinitePresentation i]
  (c : ℕ) (z : Z)

/-- A conormal sheaf of rank `c` forces the stalk of the defining ideal sheaf at `i z` to need at
least `c` generators. -/
theorem le_spanFinrank_stalkIdeal_of_conormalRank (hE : ConormalRank i c) :
    c ≤ (stalkIdeal (X := X.toLocallyRingedSpace) (definingIdealOfHom i)
      (i.base z)).spanFinrank := by
  obtain ⟨b₀⟩ := nonempty_conormalStalkBasis i c z hE
  have : IsScalarTower
      (ToType (i.coborderRange.toScheme.presheaf.stalk (i.liftCoborder.base z)))
      (ToType (Z.presheaf.stalk z))
      (RingHom.ker (i.liftCoborder.stalkMap z).hom).Cotangent :=
    ⟨fun a s m => by
      rw [Algebra.smul_def, mul_smul, RingHom.algebraMap_toAlgebra,
        cotangentStalk_smul_eq i z]⟩
  refine le_spanFinrank_of_basis_cotangent ?_ (coborderStalkRingEquiv i z)
    (map_coborderStalkRingEquiv_stalkIdeal i z) (fg_stalkIdeal_definingIdealOfHom i (i.base z))
    (b₀.map (conormalSheafStalkEquivCotangent i z))
  rw [RingHom.algebraMap_toAlgebra]
  exact i.liftCoborder.stalkMap_surjective z

/-- **A conormal sheaf of rank `c` gives a basis of the cotangent fibre indexed by `Fin c`.**
Let `i : Z ⟶ X` be a closed immersion of finite presentation whose conormal sheaf is finite
locally free of rank `c` and let `z : Z`.  Then the cotangent fibre `ℐ_x / 𝔪_x ℐ_x` of the
defining ideal sheaf at `x = i z`, a vector space over the residue field at `x`, has a basis
indexed by `Fin c`, whose vectors are the classes of `c` elements of the stalk `ℐ_x`.

This says that the *minimal* number of generators of `ℐ_x` is exactly `c`, which
`exists_stalkIdeal_eq_span_of_conormalRank` — which produces `c` generators, so an upper bound —
does not give by itself.  The lower bound is the content: it comes from the conormal sheaf, whose
stalk `ℐ/ℐ²` is free of rank `c` over the local ring of `Z` at `z`, so that no fewer than `c`
elements generate it and hence none generate `ℐ_x`.  Both bounds are compared through
`Submodule.spanFinrank`, the minimal number of generators, which
`IsLocalRing.spanFinrank_eq_finrank_quotient` identifies with the dimension of the cotangent
fibre; a spanning family of that many vectors is then a basis.

This is the shape [Stacks, Tag 067N] takes its input in, and it is what ties the `c` of the
conormal rank to the length of a Koszul-regular family cutting `Z` out. -/
theorem exists_basis_idealCotangentFiber_of_conormalRank (hE : ConormalRank i c) :
    ∃ (g : Fin c → stalkIdeal (X := X.toLocallyRingedSpace) (definingIdealOfHom i) (i.base z))
      (b : Module.Basis (Fin c)
        (ToType (X.presheaf.stalk (i.base z)) ⧸
          IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (ToType (X.presheaf.stalk (i.base z))))
        (idealCotangentFiber (X := X.toLocallyRingedSpace) (definingIdealOfHom i) (i.base z))),
      ∀ a, b a = Submodule.Quotient.mk (g a) := by
  classical
  have hfg := fg_stalkIdeal_definingIdealOfHom i (i.base z)
  obtain ⟨gg, hgg⟩ := exists_stalkIdeal_eq_span_of_conormalRank i c z hE hfg
  have hmem : ∀ a, gg a ∈ stalkIdeal (X := X.toLocallyRingedSpace) (definingIdealOfHom i)
      (i.base z) := fun a => hgg ▸ Ideal.subset_span ⟨a, rfl⟩
  -- The `c` generators bound the minimal number of generators above.
  have hle : (stalkIdeal (X := X.toLocallyRingedSpace) (definingIdealOfHom i)
      (i.base z)).spanFinrank ≤ c := by
    rw [hgg]
    refine (Submodule.spanFinrank_span_le_ncard_of_finite (Set.finite_range gg)).trans ?_
    rw [← Set.image_univ]
    simpa using Set.ncard_image_le (f := gg) (s := Set.univ) Set.finite_univ
  -- The free conormal stalk bounds it below.
  have hge := le_spanFinrank_stalkIdeal_of_conormalRank i c z hE
  -- So the cotangent fibre has dimension `c`, and the `c` generators' classes are a basis.
  have hrank : Module.finrank (ToType (X.presheaf.stalk (i.base z)) ⧸
        IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (ToType (X.presheaf.stalk (i.base z))))
      (idealCotangentFiber (X := X.toLocallyRingedSpace) (definingIdealOfHom i) (i.base z))
      = c := by
    rw [← IsLocalRing.spanFinrank_eq_finrank_quotient _ hfg]
    exact le_antisymm hle hge
  refine ⟨fun a => ⟨gg a, hmem a⟩, basisOfTopLeSpanOfCardEqFinrank
    (fun a => Submodule.Quotient.mk ⟨gg a, hmem a⟩)
    (top_le_span_range_mk _ gg hgg hmem) (by rw [Fintype.card_fin, hrank]), fun a => ?_⟩
  rw [coe_basisOfTopLeSpanOfCardEqFinrank]

end CotangentFibreBasis

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ConormalEquations

end
